        "title": "Surface Treatments and Coatings",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Surface treatments modify only the near-surface region of a part while leaving the bulk unchanged. They solve the fundamental materials engineering conflict: bulk properties (toughness, machinability) optimized for the substrate, while surface properties (hardness, wear resistance, corrosion protection) optimized independently."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-SURFACE-TREATMENT.md#003",
      "path": [
        "06-SURFACE-TREATMENT.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:materials-processing:06-surface-treatment, git-history:materials-processing:06-surface-treatment]",
        "canonical_path": "materials-processing/06-SURFACE-TREATMENT.md",
        "concepts": "[surface, treatment]",
        "current_path": "materials-processing/06-SURFACE-TREATMENT.md",
        "id": "maxim:materials-processing:surface-treatment",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "materials-processing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
